ARM: dts: BCM5301X: R7000: use port 8 as the only CPU port

The R7000 described CPU port 5 (gmac0). With port 5 the b53 driver selects
dual IMP mode (GC_FRM_MGMT_PORT_M), in which the switch delivers a VID
missing from the VLAN table to no port at all, so VLAN tagged traffic on
a port is dropped unless its VID happens to be in the table: 8021q uppers
on a VLAN-unaware bridge port never receive anything (measured on an
R7000: eth0.7 with eth0 in a bridge, 0 of 8 pings, RxDiscarded climbing).

Use port 8 (gmac2, the IMP port) alone, as the Netgear R8000/R8500,
Linksys EA9200 and D-Link DIR-885L/890L already do. With a single IMP the
switch sends table misses to the CPU and 8021q does the rest. This is the
fix the b53 maintainers asked for in the "net: dsa: b53: fix 8021q uppers
on standalone ports" thread (netdev, 2026-08/09).

b53_brcm_hdr_setup() only ever ORed the management port selection into
GC_FRM_MGMT_PORT, keeping whatever the bootloader programmed, and the CFE
of a board designed around port 5 may well have left dual IMP selected.
When port 8 is the only CPU port, select IMP0 alone.
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4709-netgear-r7000.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4709-netgear-r7000.dts
@@ -130,15 +130,25 @@
 		};
 
 		port@5 {
-			label = "cpu";
+			status = "disabled";
+
+			fixed-link {
+				speed = <1000>;
+				full-duplex;
+			};
 		};
 
 		port@7 {
 			status = "disabled";
+
+			fixed-link {
+				speed = <1000>;
+				full-duplex;
+			};
 		};
 
 		port@8 {
-			status = "disabled";
+			label = "cpu";
 		};
 	};
 };
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/b53/b53_common.c
@@ -786,10 +786,17 @@
 
 	/* Configure the appropriate IMP port */
 	b53_read8(dev, B53_MGMT_PAGE, B53_GLOBAL_CONFIG, &hdr_ctl);
-	if (port == 8)
+	if (port == 8) {
+		/* With port 8 the only CPU port, select IMP0 alone rather
+		 * than add to whatever the bootloader left: in dual IMP mode
+		 * the switch sends VIDs missing from the VLAN table nowhere.
+		 */
+		if (!dsa_is_cpu_port(ds, 5))
+			hdr_ctl &= ~GC_FRM_MGMT_PORT_M;
 		hdr_ctl |= GC_FRM_MGMT_PORT_MII;
-	else if (port == 5)
+	} else if (port == 5) {
 		hdr_ctl |= GC_FRM_MGMT_PORT_M;
+	}
 	b53_write8(dev, B53_MGMT_PAGE, B53_GLOBAL_CONFIG, hdr_ctl);
 
 	/* B53_BRCM_HDR not present on devices with legacy tags */
